  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of size NNN.\n\nThe score of a permutation PPP of the integers [1,N][1, N][1,N] is defined as follows:\n\n\nIf Pi=iP_i = iPi​=i for at least one iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N), the score is −1-1−1.\nOtherwise, the score is the number of indices iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N) such that APi≤AiA_{P_i} \\le A_iAPi​​≤Ai​.\nFind the maximum possible score for some permutation PPP. You also need to print a valid permutation.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the following:\n\n\n\nOn a new line, first output the maximum possible score.\nNext, output NNN integers, P1,P2,…,PNP_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​, any valid permutation that obtains the maximum score.\n\nIf multiple answers are possible, all will be accepted.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\le A_i \\le N1≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n1 1 1\n3\n3 1 2\n2\n2 2",
        "output": "3\n2 3 1\n2\n3 1 2\n2\n2 1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : Any permutation PPP which does not have Pi=iP_i = iPi​=i for any index iii, would have a score of 333 because all values are 111, so APi≤AiA_{P_i} \\le A_iAPi​​≤Ai​ always holds.\nTest Case 2 : P=[3,1,2]P = [3, 1, 2]P=[3,1,2] means that index i=1,3i = 1, 3i=1,3 are good because AP1=A3=2≤A1A_{P_1} = A_3 = 2 \\le A_1AP1​​=A3​=2≤A1​, and AP3=A2=1≤A3A_{P_3} = A_2 = 1 \\le A_3AP3​​=A2​=1≤A3​. It can be shown that a larger score is impossible."
      }
    ]
  },
